WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.000
One More. A workout journal built around reliable writes, quick corrections, and useful history.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:12.000
Built for the next set. Choose a workout and start a session. The same journal works on desktop and phone.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Two sets. Both saved. Record weight and reps. Identical intentional sets stay separate; request replays cannot duplicate a write.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Correct it in plain text. “Change set 2 to 7 reps.” The parser proposes the exact change and waits for confirmation.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:36.000
A correction you can trust. Set 2 now shows 7 reps. Version checks protect against stale edits, and the previous values remain in the audit log.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:43.000
Keep the context. Save setup notes alongside the numbers. Browser drafts survive reloads; saved notes live in SQLite.

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:50.000
Find the session again. Search by workout, exercise, or saved notes. This search finds the narrower-grip note and the corrected sets.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:57.000
Follow each movement. Switch between heaviest set, total volume, and reps. Sample workouts are included explicitly for this demo.

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:03.000
A journal that fits. The responsive phone layout keeps the same history and measurements. This is a browser viewport demonstration.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Transactional writes, versioned corrections, and 19 tests. Live ElevenLabs voice is not yet credential-verified.
